            <ArticleTitle>Microwave-Assisted Rapid One-Pot Synthesis of Fused and Non-Fused Indoles and 5-[18 F]Fluoroindoles from Phenylazocarboxylates.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16174-16178</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/chem.201703890</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Substituted indoles can be prepared from phenylazocarboxylates through a rapid one-pot sequence featuring a microwave-assisted Fischer indole synthesis as a key step. Considering that the phenylazocarboxylates may beforehand be modified by mild nucleophilic aromatic substitution, including the introduction of [18 F]fluoride, the overall strategy offers an attractive new access to 5-[18 F]fluoroindoles.</AbstractText>
